        "reviewed_sha": "aacea43e017db3fbd968cec390ab55a49a297bbc",
        "evidence": "Two short paragraphs; the one long sentence is broken by its parenthetical.",
        "notes": "PROOF GAP (reported, not edited). The descent argument turns on a grading of the value field that is never defined: it writes 'tr_M(T_1 T_2) - tr_M(T_2 T_1) = 0 in Q(q)_{a+b}' and then 'any T in J^{l+1} has tr_M(T) in Q(q)_{l+1}, which is strictly above the level l'. Q(q) is a field and carries no such grading in this block or its parent, and the first step is vacuous in any case (it says 0 lies in a graded piece). What the descent actually needs is tr_M(J^{l+1}) = 0, which is asserted rather than shown. The block is honestly headed 'Proof sketch', but its parent is declared proposition() and its statement claims a UNIQUELY determined trace that 'vanishes entirely' on J^{l+1} \u2014 the uniqueness and the vanishing are exactly the two things the sketch does not establish. Minor terminology: J^{l+1} is called 'the lower stratum' while being the deeper (higher-index) one."
      }
